      "title": "mpeg-sect: Fix overflow in packet_mpeg_sect_mjd_to_utc_time",
      "message": "mpeg-sect: Fix overflow in packet_mpeg_sect_mjd_to_utc_time\n\nThis could overflow even with 64-bit time_t, because the multiplicand\nand multiplier were only 32-bit values (the former after implicit\ninteger promotion).\n\nAll the times that did overflow were likely bogus, as a protocol\nusing MPEG presumably rarely refers to date earlier than can be\nrepresented even in a 32-bit time_t (though perhaps with unsigned\ntime_t.)\n\nFix #20709\n",
